# The audio here is large and mostly source material, so it stays out of the
# repo — except the lobby track. That one is the homepage: "push play on the
# lobby music" is the first thing the ring asks you to do, and Netlify builds
# from a fresh clone, so an untracked file simply would not exist in the deploy.
#
# Note this excludes the CONTENTS rather than the directory itself. Git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so "audio/" followed by
# a negation would silently keep ignoring the track.
audio/*
!audio/hwy3_lobby.mp3
